1
00:03:04,285 --> 00:03:10,285
Megan and Amy are best friends. They share secrets. They chat with guys
online. And in a few days, they will never be seen again.

2
00:06:08,571 --> 00:06:14,571
Megan Is Missing is a drama, horror, thriller film directed by Michael Goi.

3
00:09:12,857 --> 00:09:18,857
Fourteen-year–old Megan and her best friend Amy spend a lot of time on the
internet, posting videos of themselves and chatting with guys online.

4
00:12:17,142 --> 00:12:23,142
One night Megan chats with a guy named Josh who
convinces her to meet him for a date.

5
00:15:21,428 --> 00:15:27,428
The next day, Megan is missing—forever.

6
00:18:25,714 --> 00:18:31,714
Based on actual cases of child abduction.

7
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Amy Herman, played by Amber Perkins.

8
00:24:34,285 --> 00:24:40,285
Megan Stewart, played by Rachel Quinn.

9
00:27:38,571 --> 00:27:44,571
Josh, played by Dean Waite.

10
00:30:42,857 --> 00:30:48,857
Lexie, played by Jael Elizabeth Steinmeyer.

11
00:33:47,142 --> 00:33:53,142
Kathy, played by Kara Wang.

12
00:36:51,428 --> 00:36:57,428
Chelsea, played by Brittany Hingle.

13
00:39:55,714 --> 00:40:01,714
Megan Is Missing is a 2011 American found footage psychological horror film
written, directed, edited, and co-produced by Michael Goi.

14
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
The film revolves around the days leading up to the disappearance of Megan Stewart (Rachel Quinn), a popular high school student in Los Angeles who decided to
meet up with a boy she was interacting with online, and the subsequent investigation launched by her best friend Amy Herman (Amber Perkins).

15
00:46:04,285 --> 00:46:10,285
Goi based the film on a series of real-life cases of child abduction.

16
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:14,571
Marc Klaas, the founder of KlaasKids Foundation, notably endorsed the film.

17
00:52:12,857 --> 00:52:18,857
Originally developed as a low-budget independent feature in
2006, the film was shot for $30,000–35,000.

18
00:55:17,142 --> 00:55:23,142
It did not find distribution until Anchor Bay Films gave
it a limited theatrical release in 2011.

19
00:58:21,428 --> 00:58:27,428
The film was very controversial upon its release.

20
01:01:25,714 --> 01:01:31,714
Marketed as an educational film, Megan Is Missing was banned in New Zealand and has been heavily
criticized by critics for its depiction of sexual violence and brutal imagery.

21
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
Goi wrote the script in 10 days and shot the film over a week.

22
01:07:34,285 --> 01:07:40,285
Because of the graphic content, he requested that the parents of the young cast be on set
during filming so that they were fully aware of their involvement in the project.

23
01:10:38,571 --> 01:10:44,571
It is one of the first computer screen films.

24
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
The film experienced renewed popularity in 2020 after
clips of the film were shared on TikTok.

25
01:16:47,142 --> 01:16:53,142
Goi later issued public warnings to prospective viewers after many users began calling the film "traumatizing." Entertainment Weekly called it
"2011's scariest horror film." The film placed sixth in the DEG Watched at Home Top 20 Chart for Week Ending November 21, 2020.

26
01:19:51,428 --> 01:19:57,428
The film explores themes of rape, predator, based on
true story, murder, teenage girl.

27
01:22:55,714 --> 01:23:01,714
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
